<worksheet>
    <title>Week 12 LTs-B</title>
<objectives>

  <ul>
    <li>
          <p>[LT15] Given a data set, make a quadratic regression model on Desmos, identify and explain the meaning of <m>x-</m>intercepts, <m>y-</m>intercepts, and vertex in the context, find <m>f(a)</m> and explain its meaning, find <m>x</m> given <m>f(a)</m> and explain its meaning.
</p>
        </li>

        <li>
          <p>[LT16] Given a quadratic graph, find the equation in 3 different forms, identify the horizontal intercepts, vertical intercept, and vertex, evaluate <m>f(a)</m>, and find <m>x</m> given <m>f(a)</m>.
</p>
        </li>

        <li>
          <p>[LT17] Given a quadratic word situation, graph the model on Desmos, identify and explain the meaning of <m>x-</m>intercepts, <m>y-</m>intercepts, and vertex in the context, find <m>f(a)</m> and explain its meaning, find <m>x</m> given <m>f(a)</m> and explain its meaning,and determine what inputs make sense.
</p>
        </li>

        <li>
          <p>[LT18] I can recognize and identify key characteristics of a quadratic pattern represented in a table, graph, equation or application.  I can translate between different representations.</p>
        </li>


  </ul>

</objectives>

    <introduction>
    <sidebyside widths="65% 25%" valign="middle">
        <p>
            If <m>x</m> is the number of $100 bills you spend on advertising and <m>f(x)</m> represents the total revenue generated from that advertising in thousands of dollars. The table represents the relationship between the amount spent on advertising and the corresponding revenue.
        
        </p>
        <table>
            
            <tabular top="major" bottom="major" left="major" right="major">
                <row header="yes">
                    <cell><m>x</m></cell>
                    <cell><m>f(x)</m></cell>
                </row>
                <row>
                    <cell>5</cell>
                    <cell>51</cell>
                </row>
                <row>
                    <cell>6</cell>
                    <cell>71</cell>
                </row>
                <row>
                    <cell>7</cell>
                    <cell>83</cell>
                </row>
                <row>
                    <cell>9</cell>
                    <cell>76</cell>
                </row>
                <row>
                    <cell>10</cell>
                    <cell>54</cell>
                </row>
            </tabular>
        
        </table>
</sidebyside>
    </introduction>
    <exercise>
   
        <p>
           [LT15] Use Desmos to find the best fit quadratic regression model for the given data in the <alert>Standard form, Vertex form, and Factored form.</alert>
        </p>
    </exercise>
     <exercise>
            <p>
                [LT15] Use either one of the equations you obtained from the quadratic regression to calculate <m>f(8)</m>, and write a sentence to explain what this value means in the context of the problem.
            </p>     
    </exercise>
    <exercise>
            <p>[LT16] Use your graph to identify and explain the meaning of the <m>x-</m>intercepts, <m>y-</m>intercepts. Write a sentence to explain what each intercept  mean in this context.
            </p>
    </exercise>

   

   

    <exercise>
            <p>
                [LT17] How much should you spend on advertising to achieve a revenue of $80,000? Show your algebra work, and verify your answer using the graph.
            </p>
    </exercise>
 <exercise>
            <p>
                [LT18] Use your graph to determine how much you need to spend on advertising to achieve the maximum revenue, and how much is that maximum revenue.
            </p>
      </exercise>
</worksheet>